  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1052 PM CST TUE NOV 3 2026\n\nThis evening, a surface low will move out of Iowa and Wisconsin\ntoward Upper Michigan by Thursday. As it does so, it will drag a\nfront across much of the Gulf Coast States including Central\nAlabama. Shower activity will become widespread ahead of this\nfront along with a few thunderstorms with enough forcing from the\nfront. Latest guidance continues to weaken thunderstorms as they\nget closer tonight, and this agrees with the latest radar trends.\nThe flow could be a little slow at times which could yield a low\nto medium chance for heavy rain/isolated localized flooding\npotential for late tonight into Wednesday morning instead of\nsevere. The best chances would be in the NRN half of Central\nAlabama.\n\nBy Thursday, the system will continue to progress through the SE\nportions of the CWA with all precipitation expected to exit\nCentral Alabama by late Thursday evening. Behind the front on\nFriday, a much colder Canadian ridge will build to lower the\ntemperatures back into the 40s (and maybe some mid to upper 30s)\nfor lows across Central Alabama for this weekend into the first \npart of next week. Guidance is trending colder behind this front \nwith each successive run. There is a low to medium chance that we \ncould see our first frost as early as Saturday night now. This \nwould be the first of multiple days where portions of the area may\nsee frost.\n\n08",
